      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to find the measure of angle \\(\\angle CED\\) given that \\(\\angle BAE = 43^\\circ\\) and \\(AB\\) is a diameter of a circle with center \\(O\\).\n\nFirst, we note that since \\(AB\\) is a diameter, \\(\\angle ABO = 90^\\circ\\) and \\(\\angle AEB = 90^\\circ\\) because the tangent at \\(B\\) is perpendicular to the radius \\(OB\\) and the tangent at \\(E\\) is perpendicular to the radius \\(OE\\).\n\nGiven \\(\\angle BAE = 43^\\circ\\), we can find \\(\\angle ABE\\) by using the fact that the sum of angles in triangle \\(ABE\\) is \\(180^\\circ\\). Therefore, \\(\\angle ABE = 180^\\circ - \\angle BAE - \\angle AEB = 180^\\circ - 43^\\circ - 90^\\circ = 47^\\circ\\).\n\nNext, we need to find \\(\\angle CED\\). Since \\(CD\\) is a chord of the circle and \\(DE\\) is a tangent, we know that \\(\\angle CED = \\angle ABE\\) because they are alternate interior angles formed by the transversal \\(BC\\) intersecting the parallel lines \\(OE\\) and \\(CA\\). Therefore, \\(\\angle CED = 47^\\circ\\).\n\nThus, the measure of \\(\\angle CED\\) is \\(\\boxed{47}\\).",
