y), the angle BOE is 180 - 43 = 137 degrees.\nangle_BOE = 180 - angle_BAE\n\n# The tangent at B is perpendicular to OB, so angle OBE = 90 degrees.\nangle_OBE = 90\n\n# The tangent at E is perpendicular to OE, so angle OEE' = 90 degrees.\nangle_OEE_prime = 90\n\n# The tangent at E intersects AD at D, and since angle BOE = 137 degrees, angle EAD = 180 - 137 = 43 degrees.\nangle_EAD = 180 - angle_BOE\n\n# Therefore, angle CED = angle BCA + angle DEB = 90 + 90 = 180 - 43 - 43 = 90 degrees.\nangle_CED = 180 - angle_EAD - angle_BAE\n\n# Printing the result\nprint(angle_CED)\n```",
